## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **OpenAI API key** — The `.env` has `OPENAI_API_KEY=` (empty). You need to provide the real key and set `AI_PROVIDER=openai` for the real provider to activate. Until then the mock is used. Should we add a dev-friendly mode that auto-uses mock when the key is absent (current behavior) or hard-fail at startup if the provider is `openai` but no key is given?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Comic panel count** — How many panels per comic do you want? The prompt template will default to 6 panels (2 pages × 3 panels). Confirm or override.

> [!NOTE]
> **DALL-E 3 image URLs** — OpenAI returns temporary signed URLs (expire in ~60 min). The worker will immediately download and re-upload to your storage provider (MinIO/filesystem). Confirm this is the expected behavior or if you prefer storing the raw URL.

> [!NOTE]
> **Chat model** — Using `gpt-4o` for narrative planning. Config key `OPENAI_CHAT_MODEL` will be added alongside the existing `OPENAI_IMAGE_MODEL`.

## Verification Plan

### Automated
- `go build ./...` from `api/` must pass with no errors.
- `go vet ./...` must pass.

### Manual
1. Set `AI_PROVIDER=openai`, `OPENAI_API_KEY=<real-key>` in `.env`.
2. Start worker; submit a PixArt job via the UI — worker log should show `processing job` with module `pixel_portrait` and call OpenAI.
3. Submit a comic job with high/low text containing profanity — worker should fail job with `CONTENT_POLICY_VIOLATION`.
4. Submit a clean comic job — worker should step through narrative → safety → art direction → panel images → complete.
5. Mock path: remove `OPENAI_API_KEY`, restart — `mock` provider is used, no API calls made.
